	(text "DMA CLOCK REQUREMENTS\nThe Timing Control block derives internal timing\nfrom the clock input.\n\nIn 8237A systems, this input will usually be the\nw2 TTL clock from an 8224 or CLK from an 8085AH or 8284A.\n\n33% duty cycle clock generators, however, may not meet\nthe clock high time requirement of the 8237A of the\nsame frequency.\n\nFor example, 82C84A-5 CLK output violates\nthe clock high time requirement of 8237A-5. In this\ncase 82C84A CLK can simply be inverted to meet\n8237A-5 clock high and low time requirements.\n\nFor 8085AH-2 systems above 3.9 MHz, the 8085\nCLK(OUT) does not satisfy 8237A-5 clock LOW and\nHIGH time requirements. In this case, an external\nclock should be used to drive the 8237A-5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.812 42.164 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "48208474-2625-43a0-9e78-a304f2c02cf9")
	)
	(text "RAM"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 423.164 42.418 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "81b841c3-09db-4163-95a3-27e98368a75c")
	)
	(text "Address Enable: AEN enables command outputs ot the 8288\nBus Controller at least 115 ns after it becames active\n( LOW ). AEN going inactive immediately 3-states the\ncommand output drivers. AEN does not affect the I/O\ncommand lines it the 8288 is in the I/O BUS mode\n( IOB tied HIGH ).\n\nCommand Enable CEN: When this signal is LOW all 8288 command\noutputs and the DEN and PDEN control outputs are forced\nto their inactive state. When this signal is HIGH, these\nsame outputs are anbled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 174.498 181.102 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "871f51ae-164e-4ebe-9d2e-9b31cbb11d3c")
	)
	(text "Gli slot ISA 8 Bit non necessitano di ulteriori interrupt..."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 636.27 81.534 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "87a4937c-fde2-4183-a513-4392533071eb")
	)
	(text "ll segnale ~{AMWC} emette un comando di scrittura in\nmemoria in una fase precedente del ciclo macchina per\ndare ai dispositivi di memoria un'indicazione\nanticipata di un'istruzione di scrittura.\nLa sua temporizzazione è la stessa di un segnale di\ncomando di lettura.\nIl segnale ~{AMWC} è attivo basso"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.704 231.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "95eaa551-d162-45b2-b7bb-74ee94ede3fd")
	)
	(text "~{AEN} - AENBRD sono segnali complementari.\n~{AEN} = 1 - AENBRD = 0\n~{AEN} = 0 - AENBRD = 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 385.318 18.796 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a74713b6-ee7d-4e1d-ac17-8aafb10ff099")
	)
	(text "ROM"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 427.228 118.872 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e1d7cd8c-9095-4c7b-8049-253bb48b6ff8")
	)
	(text "ADDRESS ENABLE: AEN is an active LOW signal. AEN serves to\nqualify its respective Bus Ready Signal (RDY1 or RDY2).\nAEN1 validates RDY1 while AEN2 validates RDY2. Two AEN signal\ninputs are useful in system configurations which permit the\nprocessor to access two Multi-Master System Busses.\nIn non-Multi-Master configurations, the AEN signal inputs are\ntied true (LOW).\n\nBUS READY: (Transfer Complete). RDY is an active HIGH signal\nwhich is an indication from a device located on the system\ndata bus that data has been received, or is available RDY1 is\nqualified by AEN1 while RDY2 is qualified by AEN2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 94.742 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e99526ff-85a6-4cae-a70d-7859737b8319")
	)
	(text "DT/~{R}	= 1 Data Transmit / 0 Receive\nALE		= Address Latch Enable\n~{AEN}	= 0 Address Enable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.296 178.562 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f942f84f-c042-4053-b0ef-7c0b5aa37060")
	)
	(text "READY: READY is an active HIGH signal which is the synchronized\nRDY signal input. READY is cleared after the guaranteed hold\ntime to the processor has been met.\n\nREADY: is the acknowledgement from the addressed memory or I/O\ndevice that it will complete the data transfer. The RDY signal\nfrom memory or I/O is synchronized by the 8284 clock generator\nto form READY. This signal is active HIGH. The 8088 READY input\nis not synchronized. Correct operation is not guaranteed if the\nset up and hold times are not met."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.576 118.872 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fec566d6-1d2c-4636-a229-ebbaf71282dc")
	)
